c","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/!=(_:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/!=(_:_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"!=(_:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"!=","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDynamics"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDynamics"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","role":"symbol","title":"MXLDynamics","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url